# Wave W17-Y (Lake Gallant): gallant turf — lakefront turf, embankment flecks: a bright open green carrying pale embankment flecks where the shore works meet the grass, the well-kept ground of the lake of willpower (design: the embankment and shore lights ring the water; hotels, boats, and a shore that decided to be beautiful). Lake Gallant’s own ground — split from its twin Lake Insight by temperature entire (bright open water vs the frozen lake) and from Route 213’s salt flats west of it by keeping: this shore is tended, that one is weather.
